    "intro_html":  "Dak galbi is the Korean skillet dish they cook right at your table, chicken and cabbage stir fried in gochujang until the edges char and the chewy rice cakes go soft in the middle. It is loud, red, and satisfying, and it comes together in one pan on the stovetop. Each serving lands at 564 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e45 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$6.18 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
